---
// Our Story section — cream-light background, image left / copy right.
---
<section class="story section" id="story">
  <div class="container story__inner">
    <div class="story__image">
      <img src="/images/story.svg" alt="A workshop bench with tools and paint tins on a shelf" width="800" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    </div>
    <div class="story__content">
      <span class="section-num">ii.</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Two mates, a workshop, and a love of <span class="accent">well-made things.</span></h2>
      <div class="story__copy">
        <p>
          Weston started on weekends — finding tired pieces of furniture nobody
          wanted and seeing what they could become. A chipped sideboard. A
          bedside table missing a handle. A chest of drawers headed for the skip.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every piece we put out has been stripped, sanded, and finished by hand.
          We work with chalk-based paints, hand-waxed wooden tops, and quality
          fixings — the kind of details that make a piece last another fifty years.
        </p>
        <p>It's not mass-produced. It's not perfect. That's the point.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .story {
    background: var(--cream-light);
  }
  .story__inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .story__image {
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .story__image img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }
  .story__content { max-width: 34rem; }
  .story h2 { margin-top: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 1.75rem; }
  .story__copy p {
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
    color: rgba(46, 46, 46, 0.82);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .story__copy p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .story__inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
